ieces  together while watching of where we were  headed I held on to the last breath with  Eliot as he tried to fight away the  realization with pain and her voice that  echoes the pain of the situation and  what was going on what's happening in  that room Christa asks did your father  sexually molest you he replies yes as if  it's only in that exact moment that he's  understanding that that is the  unbearable truth it's a rare moment in a  TV show that's so heavily theorized  about and broken down like every detail  that a twist like this can come together  it's not that people haven't made  theories about Edward being a bad person  or the idea of Elliot being a victim of  abuse hasn't been out there but it  hasn't felt like it's been on the  collective radar in relation to the end  game and yet here we are I really didn't  see this coming and it hit me like a ton  of bricks to be honest I think it goes  without saying that it was handled well  and in a way that felt genuine the  acting by everyone involved matched the  gravity of the reveal and rami malek  really outdid himself in his portrayal  of this character touching that part of  himself that he's kept buried for all  these years  it was magnificent the episode doesn't  end there though Vera has one more part  to play as he reveals to Elliot that his  is the thing that makes him important he  tells Elliot that he was molested as a  child as well and tells him he can find  an untapped source of strength in what's  happened once you've weathered a storm  like yours he says you become the storm  you hear me you are the storm and it's  the rest of the world that needs to run  for cover the interaction between Elliot  and Vera has its own merits but it's  really just the setup for Vera's end  just as it's looking like Fernando is  getting what he wanted to be the one to  bring Elliot back up after he's been  broken down Krista plunges a knife into  his back killing him in how it shot it  almost works as a twist in of itself in  that only after it happens we realized  that Elliot must have seen her coming  and that more than engaging with what  Barrow was saying he was just trying to  keep him from noticing she was there he  falls to the ground the lights go out  symbolically one by one and the five act  play comes to an end  it's a gripping hour of television that  takes all the boxes of greatness as a  standalone piece of art the acting the  soundtrack and the camerawork are all  turned up to 11 the music is so good it  even elevates Vera's monologuing at  times in a way that I wouldn't have  thought was possible it also answers one  major question that we've had for a long  time what happened that day with the  window did Edward push Elliot or did he  jump now we know mr. robot took over and  that he did in fact jump but the  horrible things his father did actually  play a part in pushing him out that  window it's crazy because this is an  answer that asks a lot more questions  and it's coming to us late in the game  as much as I love this episode on its  own I have to wonder how it relates to  this story coming to a close part of the  reason Elliot went after Ecore was to  avenge his father's death and now we're  left wondering how much of that was even  real the mr. robot alter who he created  for protection also looks like his  father so what will that mean for their  relationship going ahead I mean for what  it's worth mr. robot isn't his father in  fact he's the father he never had which  is clear after the reveal but the way  things were left and at least felt like  robot couldn't protect him anymore so  what will that actually mean the truth  is based on the fact that season 4 is  half way over at this point we just  don't know  it's daring which I like but it's also a  little scary which I don't like my hope  is that it all makes sense when seen as  a whole and my faith really hasn't been  shook here because I have been enjoying  each episode as they come I wasn't  excited about Vera returning and that  turned out swimmingly so there's no need  to worry right I mean historically I've  enjoyed the risks that mr. robot has  taken maybe more than some people so I  really do find that a lot more exciting  than I do worrying but I mean there's a  lot of balls in the air and the season  opened with only eight more days for  Elliot to live and we don't seem to be  getting to the part where we figure out  what it's all about like I said I'd like  that they're taking chances and they're  making some really great episodes and I  just hope that it all works out to  combine into something that will really  give us a memorable ending I'm really  interested to see what you guys think -  let me know in the comments about what  you think about Episode seven by itself  and season four as a whole how do we  think this reveal changes things that  we've taken for granted for so long at  this point in the story I don't think  we've seen the last of mr. robot because  Elliot would need him now more than ever  at the same time it's hard to not see  him as Edward Alderson and to rewrite  all those good dad memories we've  associated with him and what about the  other how does the third alter fit into  the mix now that things have been turned  on their heads with number one and  number two also how to start lean fit  into all of this I tend to think that  she didn't know about what happened to  Elliot but I really don't know if that's  just because that's what I want to be  true I would have to go back and  re-watch the whole thing to get a better  idea of how they interacted if Edward  abused Elliot then we have to wonder  about Darlene and even Angela for that  matter it's a lot to process and I think  that I'm just gonna leave it there let  me know what you think in the comments  please like this video if you enjoyed it  and subscribe to my channel if you  haven't already we're officially halfway  through the final season of mr. robot  thanks for watching I'll talk to you  soon
 

